BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-therma-fish-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-therma-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271102
SUMMARY:Fish panigiri of Agioi Anargyroi\, Therma
LOCATION:Therma\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The spa village of Therma\, next to Agios Kirykos\, keeps the November feast of Agioi Anargyroi (1 November) as a psaropanigiro: fish and seafood instead of goat\, wine\, and island music by the little harbour. A winter-season curiosity for anyone on Ikaria for the hot springs\; the summer version of the same saints is on 30 June-1 July.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#therma-fish-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-therma
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#therma-fish-panigiri-of-agioi-anargyroi-therma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fournoi-kamari-panigiri-of-the-taxiarches-kamari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Taxiarches\, Kamari
LOCATION:Kamari\, Fournoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The off-season panigiri of Fournoi: on the eve of the Archangels (7 November) the hamlet of Kamari\, over the hill from the port\, holds vespers and then a village feast with traditional meat dishes. Small\, wintry and entirely local\; the monastery of Agios Minas follows with its own feast on 11 November.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#kamari-panigiri-of-the-taxiarches-kamari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#kamari-panigiri-of-the-taxiarches-kamari
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iraklia-agios-nektarios-panagia-feast-of-the-taxiarches-and-agios-ne-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Feast of the Taxiarches and Agios Nektarios
LOCATION:Agios Nektarios / Panagia\, Iraklia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Two feasts back to back in November: the Archangels on 8 November and Agios Nektarios on the 9th at the chapel of the same name\, each with a liturgy and a meal in the churchyard for the islanders who stay through winter. Only for the committed off-season visitor.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#agios-nektarios-panagia-feast-of-the-taxiarches-and-agios-ne
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#agios-nektarios-panagia-feast-of-the-taxiarches-and-agios-ne
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nisyros-emporios-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-emporios-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Taxiarchis\, Emporios
LOCATION:Emporios\, Nisyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Emporios\, the half-abandoned village on the crater rim\, comes alive on 7-8 November for the Archangel Michael with a vespers and a feast in the little square\, and again on 8 September for the Nativity of the Virgin. A winter feast for those who love the island empty.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#emporios-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-emporios
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#emporios-panigiri-of-taxiarchis-emporios
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rethymno-arkadi-commemoration-of-the-arkadi-holocaust-arkadi-monaster-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Commemoration of the Arkadi holocaust\, Arkadi Monastery
LOCATION:Arkadi\, Crete (Rethymno)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Each 8 November the monastery and the Region of Crete mark the 1866 siege in which the defenders blew up the powder store rather than surrender: a memorial liturgy\, wreath-laying at the ossuary\, speeches and a parade of the local schools and associations\, with vespers and events the evening before. The Rethymno–Arkadi road is busy that morning\; go early and see the church and the powder-store ruin before the ceremony.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#arkadi-commemoration-of-the-arkadi-holocaust-arkadi-monaster
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#arkadi-commemoration-of-the-arkadi-holocaust-arkadi-monaster
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-galani-feast-of-the-taxiarches-moni-taxiarchon-galani-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Feast of the Taxiarches\, Moni Taxiarchon (Galani)
LOCATION:Galani\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's patron feast at the fortified 16th-century Taxiarches monastery near Galani\, in the north: vespers on 7 November and liturgy on the 8th\, with a communal meal for everyone who makes the trip and Serifiots returning from Athens. It is the one off-season event worth planning a visit around — but check ferry schedules\, as November crossings are few and weather-dependent.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#galani-feast-of-the-taxiarches-moni-taxiarchon-galani
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#galani-feast-of-the-taxiarches-moni-taxiarchon-galani
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:symi-panormitis-feast-of-panormitis-taxiarchis-michail-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271109
SUMMARY:Feast of Panormitis (Taxiarchis Michail)
LOCATION:Panormitis\, Symi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Patron saint feast at the cliffside Monastery of Archangel Michael at Panormitis bay. Pilgrims arrive from across the Dodecanese\; the saint is said to grant wishes left in messages tied to floating bottles.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#panormitis-feast-of-panormitis-taxiarchis-michail
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#panormitis-feast-of-panormitis-taxiarchis-michail
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aegina-saint-nektarios-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271110
SUMMARY:Saint Nektarios
LOCATION:Aegina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Major pilgrimage to the monastery where the saint lived and is buried — one of the most venerated saints in Greek Orthodoxy. Thousands come from the mainland.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#saint-nektarios
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#saint-nektarios
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salamis-salamina-town-feast-of-agios-minas-patron-salamina-town-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271112
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Minas (patron)\, Salamina Town
LOCATION:Salamina Town\, Salamina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Minas is the patron of Salamina and his metropolitan church in the town centre keeps 10-11 November with vespers\, an episcopal liturgy by the Metropolitan of Megara and Salamina and a procession of the icon through the streets\, followed by the town's autumn fair. Twenty minutes from Piraeus by ferry\, so an easy half-day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#salamina-town-feast-of-agios-minas-patron-salamina-town
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#salamina-town-feast-of-agios-minas-patron-salamina-town
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hydra-hydra-town-feast-of-agios-konstantinos-o-ydraios-patron-hydr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271116
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Konstantinos o Ydraios (patron)\, Hydra Town
LOCATION:Hydra Town\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Hydra's own saint is Konstantinos the New Martyr\, born on the island around 1770 and executed in Rhodes in 1800\; his relics lie in the cathedral of the Panagia on the harbour\, and 13-15 November is the island's biggest religious weekend\, with vespers on the 13th\, an episcopal liturgy and a procession of the relics round the port on the 14th. Off-season\, so the island is quiet and cheap\; the Metropolitan of Hydra presides and the port cafés fill after the procession.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#hydra-town-feast-of-agios-konstantinos-o-ydraios-patron-hydr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#hydra-town-feast-of-agios-konstantinos-o-ydraios-patron-hydr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-chozoviotissa-monastery-chora-feast-of-panagia-chozoviotissa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271122
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Chozoviotissa (Presentation of the Virgin)
LOCATION:Chozoviotissa Monastery\, Chora\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Feast of the Presentation at the dramatic clifftop monastery. Smaller crowds than 15 August festivals elsewhere — proper local atmosphere.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#chozoviotissa-monastery-chora-feast-of-panagia-chozoviotissa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#chozoviotissa-monastery-chora-feast-of-panagia-chozoviotissa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kimolos-chorio-feast-of-panagia-odigitria-chorio-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271122
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Odigitria\, Chorio
LOCATION:Chorio\, Kimolos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The patroness of Kimolos\, Panagia Odigitria\, is celebrated at the big 1867 church in Chorio on the Presentation of the Virgin: vespers on 20 November\, a bishop's liturgy and procession of the icon on the 21st\, and a traditional glenti afterwards. It's the island's most important religious day\, attended by Kimolians who come back from Athens for it\; expect a cold wind and very few tavernas open.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-feast-of-panagia-odigitria-chorio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-feast-of-panagia-odigitria-chorio
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-kounistra-monastery-troulos-panigiri-of-panagia-kounistra-ei-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271122
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Kounistra (Eikonistria)\, Kounistra Monastery
LOCATION:Kounistra Monastery (Troulos)\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Skiathos' patroness is honoured on 21 November (Eisodia)\, and the real event is the night before: islanders drive or walk the 8 km through the pine forest to the fortified monastery above Troulos\, keep vigil and sit around fires lit in the courtyard until the morning liturgy. It is a winter feast\, so expect wool coats\, tsipouro and simple food rather than a tourist show. Bring a torch and warm clothes\; parking on the monastery track is limited so arrive early on the 20th.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#kounistra-monastery-troulos-panigiri-of-panagia-kounistra-ei
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#kounistra-monastery-troulos-panigiri-of-panagia-kounistra-ei
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sikinos-chora-eisodia-tis-theotokou-fish-soup-feast-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20271121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271122
SUMMARY:Eisodia tis Theotokou fish-soup feast\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Sikinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 21 November the village gathers in the square of Chora for a meal of psarosoupa (fish soup) offered by the year's sponsor\, who keeps the icon at home until the next feast. A winter tradition for the few hundred residents rather than a tourist event\, but a genuine one\; ferries in November are sparse\, so it's for those already on the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#chora-eisodia-tis-theotokou-fish-soup-feast-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#chora-eisodia-tis-theotokou-fish-soup-feast-chora
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
